On the subject of Wishes granted by Shopkeepers- How about no wishes from
normal shopkeepers, but perhaps a speical shop similar to the Oracle- that only
appears on large dungeon levels or something and sells really awesome stuff
Like Multiple Artifacts with different outrageous plusses or strange
properites... You see- more-
+17 Cursed Broadsword named Stormbringer of Fumbling- more
+1 Blessed Rustproofed Longsword named Henry IV -more
Blessed Bag of Frito Layes Potatoe Grenades -more
-2 Cursed Shortsword Named Excalibur of Destruction -more
This shop would only appear at low levels and the prices would be outrageous-
The Proprietor would be a Wiard or a Shamen and would be extremely hard to
kill. With an Armor class of 300 and 5000 Hp. He would hardly ever get angry at
you and it would be almost impossible to steal from the store- (Very hard walls
and no pets allowed.) You might be able to smuggle a pet figurine in or
something. 
	The Wizard might also accept Stats as payment for the items.
As you leave the Shop without paying Effrax taps you lightly on the shoulder
and smiles. You would then be able to leave but without a couple of points of 
an important stat. To keep the pets out the doorway might be cursed or perhaps
all the things in the shop would be cursed (gathered from esoteric corpses)
and you might have to uncurse them to use them well. Some of the things in the
shop might be really acctually garbage but with nice names like the special
store in the Third book of Faferd and the Grey Mouse by Fritz Leiber. 
	Tell me what you all think?
 
